  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY NIGHT THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 1257 PM MDT Thu May 28 2026\n\nWarmer and drier conditions are still expected to set in this \nweekend as the upper low moves off to the northeast. Temperatures \nwill remain in the 70s-80s across the area on Saturday, with hottest \nconditions over the eastern plains. On Sunday, temperatures increase \na few degrees across the board, with some areas out east exceeding \n90. With the low moving out of our area, and dry air in place across \nthe region, precip chances remain near zero in our CWA.\n\nLate Sunday into early Monday, a weak cool front will move south \nacross the plains, bringing back some low level moisture and upslope \nflow over the I-25 corridor. This indicated the beginning of a \nslightly cooler and wetter pattern as we move into next week, though \nmodel agreement is still low. A series of shortwaves will pass \nthrough the flow over our region, leading to generally unsettled \nconditions, but timing is still too uncertain to narrow down the \ndetails.",
